{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"e33c29bbc82d3c88d6cfcc90aeaf814b85d085b0; 21/21 passing. Root causes: (1) fetch --set-upstream configured the wrong branch (derived from fetched ref instead of current HEAD); rewrote as apply_set_upstream() mirroring builtin/fetch.c (config current branch; merge=single FETCH_HEAD-only source ref, HEAD for anon URL; skip refspecs with :dst; tag/multi-branch/detached warnings). (2) pull had no --set-upstream/--tags; added flags, forwarded to fetch and to local-path/pull-. shortcuts. (3) pull HEAD eager-resolution bailed for bare-relative remote url; now leaves HEAD for fetch. (4) git pull <remote> <src>:<dst> had no merge candidate; mark_cli_refspecs_for_merge() promotes CLI-refspec branch lines. (5) set_upstream must run before the ref-update-failure bail so config is set even on lock conflict (t5510 #213, still 215/215). Regressions checked clean: t5510,t5520,t5521,t5524,t5574,t5582. NOTE: t5515-fetch-merge-logic and t5572-pull-submodule are failing from ANOTHER agent's in-flight promisor_hydrate.rs work (peeled ^{} tags / missing-object copy), NOT this change."}